\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Cost of the sea ice relative to the standard scheme, for the schemes that survive Sect.~6.4. Negative is a saving. The measure is the ice cost --- ice, ice dynamics and ice advection, computation together with time spent waiting for communication --- and not the model time step, which divides an ice-only change by about ten. Each mesh is at its own operating point, the largest node count at which the model still gains from more GPUs, read off the measured strong-scaling curve of the standard scheme; each was measured in a single allocation with all configurations run back to back. Both wide-halo bars are exact and reproduce the standard trajectory bit for bit.}}{4}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:meshes}{{1}{4}{Cost of the sea ice relative to the standard scheme, for the schemes that survive Sect.~6.4. Negative is a saving. The measure is the ice cost --- ice, ice dynamics and ice advection, computation together with time spent waiting for communication --- and not the model time step, which divides an ice-only change by about ten. Each mesh is at its own operating point, the largest node count at which the model still gains from more GPUs, read off the measured strong-scaling curve of the standard scheme; each was measured in a single allocation with all configurations run back to back. Both wide-halo bars are exact and reproduce the standard trajectory bit for bit}{figure.caption.9}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Difference in ice thickness against a run exchanging after every sub-cycle, fArc on 16 GPUs after 60 days, with the 16 sub-domain boundaries drawn on top and a common colour scale. The delayed exchange (left) leaves a difference that follows the boundaries; the exact wide halo (right) does not, and differs from the reference only in the order of summation.}}{8}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:artefact}{{2}{8}{Difference in ice thickness against a run exchanging after every sub-cycle, fArc on 16 GPUs after 60 days, with the 16 sub-domain boundaries drawn on top and a common colour scale. The delayed exchange (left) leaves a difference that follows the boundaries; the exact wide halo (right) does not, and differs from the reference only in the order of summation}{figure.caption.13}{}}
